# Widths, wide characters at the margins, combining marks, ZWJ
# sequences, flags and variation selectors, with mode 2027 off and on.
@cite https://www.unicode.org/reports/tr11/

@case A wide character at the last column wraps
@size 10x2
@send "\e[1;10H日"
@expect-screen
|··········|
|日‹········|
@expect-cursor 2,3

@case A wide character in column 9 fits
@size 10x2
@send "\e[1;9H日"
@expect-screen
|········日‹|
@expect-cursor 1,10

@case Wide characters take two cells
@size 10x2
@send "日本語"
@expect-screen
|日‹本‹語‹····|

@case Emoji are wide
@size 10x2
@send "\u{1F600}x"
@expect-screen
|😀‹x·······|

@case Overwriting the right half clears the left
@size 10x2
@send "日\e[1;2Hx"
@expect-screen
|·x········|

@case Overwriting the left half clears the right
@size 10x2
@send "日\e[1;1Hx"
@expect-screen
|x·········|

@case A combining mark joins the previous cell
@size 10x2
@send "e\u{301}x"
@expect-screen
|éx········|
@expect-cursor 1,3

@case A combining mark joins a wide character
@size 10x2
@send "日\u{301}"
@expect-screen
|日́‹········|

@case A combining mark after a pending wrap joins the last column
@size 10x2
@send "\e[1;10Ha\u{301}"
@expect-screen
|·········á|
@expect-cursor 1,10

@case A combining mark at column 1 of an empty row is dropped
@size 10x2
@send "\u{301}a"
@expect-screen
|a·········|

@case ZWJ without mode 2027 keeps two emoji
@size 10x2
@send "\u{1F468}\u{200D}\u{1F469}"
@expect-screen
|👨‍‹👩‹······|

@case ZWJ with mode 2027 makes one cluster
@size 10x2
@mode-2027 on
@send "\u{1F468}\u{200D}\u{1F469}"
@expect-screen
|👨‍👩‹········|
@expect-cursor 1,3

@case Flags without mode 2027 are two narrow cells
@size 10x2
@send "\u{1F1FA}\u{1F1F8}"
@expect-screen
|🇺🇸········|

@case Flags with mode 2027 are one wide cluster
@size 10x2
@mode-2027 on
@send "\u{1F1FA}\u{1F1F8}"
@expect-screen
|🇺🇸‹········|

@case VS16 with mode 2027 widens
@size 10x2
@mode-2027 on
@send "\u{2764}\u{FE0F}x"
@expect-screen
|❤️‹x·······|

@case VS16 without mode 2027 stays narrow
@size 10x2
@send "\u{2764}\u{FE0F}x"
@expect-screen
|❤️x········|

@case Hangul jamo cluster with mode 2027
@size 10x2
@mode-2027 on
@send "\u{1112}\u{1161}\u{11AB}x"
@expect-screen
|한‹x·······|

@case Devanagari conjunct with mode 2027 is one cell
@size 10x2
@mode-2027 on
@send "\u{915}\u{94D}\u{937}\u{93F}x"
@expect-screen
|क्षिx········|

@case Ambiguous characters are narrow by default
@size 10x2
@send "\u{B0}x"
@expect-screen
|°x········|

@case DECRQM reports mode 2027
@size 10x2
@send "\e[?2027$p"
@expect-reply "\e[?2027;2$y"
